<title>NETHERLANDS: FORECAST - DUTCH OCT CPI SEEN UP 2.1 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - DUTCH OCT CPI SEEN UP 2.1 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bank economists expect Dutch</p>
<p>October consumer price inflation to pick up to a year-on-year</p>
<p>rate of 2.1 percent from 2.0 percent in September.</p>
<p>The October consumer inflation data is due to be published</p>
<p>at 0930 GMT on Friday. Economists' forecasts, collected by</p>
<p>Reuters, are summarised below:</p>
<p>GMT---Date--Period--Indicator----Consensus--Range------Pvs</p>
<p> 0830  8/11  Oct     CPI mth/mth  +0.1 pct   0.0/0.2  +0.9</p>
<p> 0830  8/11  Oct     CPI yr/yr    +2.1 pct   2.0/2.3  +2.0</p>
<p>Forecasts contributed by: ABN AMRO, ING, Generale Bank,</p>
<p>MeesPierson, Rabobank.</p>
<p>-- Andrew Kelly, Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
